## aborted / re-queued
- launch_hypA12k.sh killed 11:12: pred_tmp path collided with the concurrent
  wave3 job (both wrote hypA/pred_tmp/<lut>.npy).  Fixed by tag-scoping pred_tmp
  and making gt_tmp writes atomic in run_e1_on_a0.py / ablate_a0.py; re-queued
  as wave5.  Lesson: concurrent runs sharing an outdir need per-tag temp dirs.
- 5 concurrent GPU jobs starved each other (each is kernel-launch bound, not
  compute bound).  Converged to: critical path first, later waves poll the
  previous wave's done marker.
